		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[George Harrison]]></title>
			<link>//george-harrison/</link>
			<pubDate>Wed, 02 Oct 2024 12:08:35 +0000</pubDate>
			<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">/?p=6</guid>
			<description></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:group {"layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group"><!-- wp:block-development-examples/interactivity-router-2f43f8 {"next":"ringo-starr", "prev":"john-lennon"} -->
<div class="wp-block-block-development-examples-interactivity-router-2f43f8"><!-- wp:columns -->
<div class="wp-block-columns"><!-- wp:column -->
<div class="wp-block-column"><!-- wp:image {"id":53,"sizeSlug":"full","linkDestination":"none"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/WordPress/block-development-examples/trunk/plugins/interactivity-router-2f43f8/_playground/images/george-harrison.webp" alt="" class="wp-image-53"/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image --></div>
<!-- /wp:column -->

<!-- wp:column -->
<div class="wp-block-column"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>George Harrison</strong> was a British musician, singer, and songwriter best known as the lead guitarist of <strong>The Beatles</strong>. Often referred to as "The Quiet Beatle," Harrison's talent as a songwriter blossomed later in the band's career, contributing iconic songs like "Here Comes the Sun," "Something," and "While My Guitar Gently Weeps."</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:column --></div>
<!-- /wp:columns --></div>
<!-- /wp:block-development-examples/interactivity-router-2f43f8 --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After The Beatles disbanded, Harrison launched a successful solo career, releasing the critically acclaimed triple album <em>All Things Must Pass</em>, which included the hit single "My Sweet Lord." He became known for his spiritual lyrics, drawing inspiration from Eastern philosophy and Indian music, which he famously introduced to Western audiences by incorporating sitar into The Beatles' songs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Harrison was also a pioneer in organizing large-scale charity events with his <em>Concert for Bangladesh</em> in 1971, influencing future humanitarian efforts in music. He continued to release music through his solo career and as a member of the supergroup <strong>Traveling Wilburys</strong>. Harrison passed away in 2001, but his legacy as a musician and spiritual seeker endures.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
			<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded>
